Keep firefox_activate listed after activation

ListTools returns the gateway tool only while `isActivated` is false, and
`firefox_activate` lives in GATEWAY_TOOLS rather than TOOLS. Once any category
is activated the gateway disappears from the tool list for the rest of the
session, so a client that activated a narrow category can never widen it.

This bites hardest with "diagnose", whose CATEGORY_GROUPS entry is ['diagnose']
and does not pull in 'core': the session is left with firefox_diagnose as its
only reachable tool. The ACTIVATION_REQUIRED recovery path in CallTool does not
help, because a client cannot call a tool whose schema was never advertised.

The CallTool handler already processes firefox_activate unconditionally, ahead
of every activation check, so simply keeping it listed is enough to make
widening work.

--- a/mcp/server.js
+++ b/mcp/server.js
@@ -1408,7 +1408,10 @@
     availableTools = availableTools.filter(tool => tool.name !== 'firefox_navigate');
   }
 
-  return { tools: availableTools };
+  // Keep the gateway listed so a later call can widen the activated set: a
+  // session that activated a narrow category (e.g. "diagnose") would otherwise
+  // lose firefox_activate for good and never reach the browser tools.
+  return { tools: [...GATEWAY_TOOLS, ...availableTools] };
 });
 
 // Handle tool calls
